  "topology_reason": "Two HQ edge routers connect 4 remote sites. Routed links keep broadcasts local; 802.1Q trunks are limited to each access switch's VLAN and unused native VLAN 999. Rapid-PVST (RSTP per VLAN) protects local L2 wiring. Independent spoke links to both hubs provide dual-homed path failover. 48-port access switches are counted from planned endpoints, with one VLAN per switch.",
  "address_summary": {
    "reserved_addresses": 4184,
    "root_addresses": 65536,
    "root_reserved_percent": 6.38,
    "reason": "Each site's VLAN blocks are placed largest-first inside an aligned site aggregate. Site aggregates and /30 transit blocks are then placed largest-first in the root. Aggregates are reservations, not extra active subnets."
  },
  "warnings": [
    "Configurations target a lab IOS/IOS XE feature set. Match interface names and supported commands to the chosen image before pasting.",
    "End hosts use static addresses; DHCP, DNS, Internet access and NAT are outside this lab.",
    "One distribution switch and one router at each remote site remain single points of failure.",
    "CloudVPC is an IOS cloud-gateway emulator, not an actual provisioned cloud VPC.",
    "Both hub routers share one simulated provider. Separate carrier fault domains must be provisioned to protect against provider failure.",
    "WAN IPsec/IKEv2 and BGP require GNS3/CML with a suitable licensed IOS XE image. Packet Tracer support is incomplete."
  ]
}
